# Production source of truth

`https://rtikhonov.com` is a **Cloudflare Worker** that serves the Astro app in `rtikhonov.com/`.

## Do this first when the user says something is missing / not live

1. `curl -sI` / `curl -sL` the live URL (and the homepage HTML).
2. Confirm host: Cloudflare (`cf-ray`, `server: cloudflare`) vs GitHub Pages.
3. Diff live HTML against `rtikhonov.com/` — not against a stale mental model of `main`.

Pushing to GitHub does **not** publish. Prod updates only via `npm run deploy` in `rtikhonov.com/` (Wrangler).

## Wrong tree (common trap)

| Location | Role |
| :--- | :--- |
| `rtikhonov.com/` on the Cloudflare hosting lineage | **Live site** (Work gallery, era timeline, Inspiration flag, Wrangler) |
| Repo-root Astro on `main` / GitHub Pages | **Not** what DNS serves today — do not “fix” live bugs there |

If `main` has a feature but live does not, port it onto the Cloudflare site tree and deploy. Do not spend turns polishing `main` for a Cloudflare DNS site.

## Branching

Prefer branching from the branch that last powered prod (often `cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting` or the current Workers-based feature branch), not from an outdated Pages-only `main`, unless the user says otherwise.
